#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Creating a Client\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:18
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<TabGroup defaultValue=\"ts\">\n"
"  <TabList>\n"
"    <Tab value=\"ts\">TypeScript</Tab>\n"
"    <Tab value=\"go\">Go</Tab>\n"
"  </TabList>\n"
"  <TabPanels>\n"
"    <TabPanel value=\"ts\">\n"
"    The first step when working with AT data is authenticating. You can authenticate using any [OAuth](/guides/auth) provider, or with [PasswordAgent](https://github.com/bluesky-social/atproto/tree/main/packages/lex/lex-password-agent) from our SDK if you are using password auth.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:20 src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "    Begin by installing the ATProto SDK packages:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:27
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    npm install @atproto/lex @atproto/lex-password-agent\n"
"    ```\n"
"    </TabPanel>\n"
"    <TabPanel value=\"go\">\n"
"    The first step when working with AT data is authenticating. You can authenticate using any [OAuth](/guides/auth) provider, or with password authentication from our SDK.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:36
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    go get github.com/bluesky-social/indigo\n"
"    ```\n"
"    </TabPanel>\n"
"  </TabPanels>\n"
"</TabGroup>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:38
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because AT uses regular HTTP verbs and HTTP endpoints, you can also follow this guide by using a CLI tool like cURL to make HTTP requests following the [HTTP Reference](https://docs.bsky.app/docs/category/http-reference) endpoints. Most users will want to use an SDK.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Password Authentication\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you are using password auth, you should generate an [app password](/specs/xrpc#app-passwords) for your account rather than using your main account password. If you are using Bluesky as an auth provider, you can generate an app password in your [account settings](https://bsky.app/settings/app-passwords).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:51
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<TabGroup defaultValue=\"ts\">\n"
"  <TabList>\n"
"    <Tab value=\"ts\">TypeScript</Tab>\n"
"    <Tab value=\"go\">Go</Tab>\n"
"  </TabList>\n"
"  <TabPanels>\n"
"    <TabPanel value=\"ts\">\n"
"    Start by importing `PasswordAgent`, providing credentials to `PasswordAgent.login()`, and creating an `agent`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:54
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```tsx\n"
"    import { PasswordAgent } from '@atproto/lex-password-agent'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:60
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    const result = await PasswordAgent.login({\n"
"      service: 'https://bsky.social', // or your PDS host\n"
"      identifier: 'your-handle.bsky.social',\n"
"      password: 'your-app-password',\n"
"    })\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:65
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    if (result.success) {\n"
"        const agent = result.value\n"
"    }\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:70
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    Applications with an end user login flow should use [OAuth](/guides/auth) authentication rather than app password sessions. Password auth is acceptable for bots and command line tools. Both methods will produce the same authenticated `agent`.\n"
"    </TabPanel>\n"
"    <TabPanel value=\"go\">\n"
"    Start by importing the `atproto` and `xrpc` libraries, creating an `&xrpc.Client{}`, and providing credentials to call `ServerCreateSession()`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:77
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```go\n"
"    import (\n"
"      \"context\"\n"
"      comatproto \"github.com/bluesky-social/indigo/api/atproto\"\n"
"      \"github.com/bluesky-social/indigo/xrpc\"\n"
"    )\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:80
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    func main() {\n"
"      ctx := context.Background()\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:84
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      client := &xrpc.Client{\n"
"        Host: \"https://bsky.social\", // or your PDS host\n"
"      }\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:94
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      session, _ := comatproto.ServerCreateSession(ctx, client, &comatproto.ServerCreateSession_Input{\n"
"        Identifier: \"your-handle.bsky.social\",\n"
"        Password:   \"your-app-password\",\n"
"      })\n"
"    }\n"
"    ```\n"
"    </TabPanel>\n"
"  </TabPanels>\n"
"</TabGroup>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:96
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "## Client Sessions\n"
msgstr "<Heading level={2} id=\"collection\">コレクション</Heading>"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:105
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<TabGroup defaultValue=\"ts\">\n"
"  <TabList>\n"
"    <Tab value=\"ts\">TypeScript</Tab>\n"
"    <Tab value=\"go\">Go</Tab>\n"
"  </TabList>\n"
"  <TabPanels>\n"
"    <TabPanel value=\"ts\">\n"
"    Once you have a logged-in `agent`, you can create a `Client` instance to read and write data:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:109
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```tsx\n"
"    import { Client } from '@atproto/lex'\n"
"    const client = new Client(agent)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:116
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Make authenticated API calls\n"
"    console.log('Logged in as:', agent.did)\n"
"    ```\n"
"    </TabPanel>\n"
"    <TabPanel value=\"go\">\n"
"    Once you have an authed `client`, you can store auth info and make API calls:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:125
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```go\n"
"    // Store auth info on the client for subsequent requests\n"
"    client.Auth = &xrpc.AuthInfo{\n"
"      AccessJwt:  session.AccessJwt,\n"
"      RefreshJwt: session.RefreshJwt,\n"
"      Handle:     session.Handle,\n"
"      Did:        session.Did,\n"
"    }\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:131
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    fmt.Printf(\"Logged in as: %s (%s)\\n\", session.Handle, session.Did)\n"
"    ```\n"
"    </TabPanel>\n"
"  </TabPanels>\n"
"</TabGroup>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:133
#, no-wrap
msgid "From here, you can go directly to [making API requests](/guides/reads-and-writes).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:135
#, no-wrap
msgid "## API Tokens\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:137
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rate limits for logging in are generally lower than for other API operations. Calling the login method multiple times in a short period may trigger rate limits. You only need to call the login method once per session to authenticate your agent.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:141
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `com.atproto.server.createSession` API endpoint called by login methods returns a session object containing two API tokens:\n"
"* `accessJwt`: an access token which is used to authenticate requests but expires after a few minutes\n"
"* `refreshJwt`: a refresh token which lasts longer and is used only to update the session with a new access token\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/sdk-auth/en.mdx:143
#, no-wrap
msgid "The SDK stores this session information for you, and will include it in the headers of its requests.\n"
msgstr ""

